Sometimes reading the monster combat code teaches good
tactics.  Throw everythnig throwable as you advance and only
switch to wielding a melee weapon when all of the throwing and
shooting and zapping has been done.

Sometimes reading the monster code teaches more than what
monsters do.  If I don't have a bow and I do have a stack of
arrows, I start throwing them at oncoming monsters as soon as
they come in range and I've run out of other stuff to throw at
them.  I'll also throw weaker stuff at weaker monsters so I
might throw arrows at orcs but daggers at trolls or whatever.

Also, monsters that throw should prefer throwing the missiles
that have been thrown at them.  Player missiles are stronger
than monster missiles because of gradual enchantment.  Not
true in every case but true often enough to make it good tactics.

